file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h1_dataset.dta saved

.         
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS *
.  
. *We include only families with 1-2 children. If participants had children dur
> ing our included panel years, this was reflected in sumkids but not biokids, 
> so we use sumkids as our basis for exclusion.
. drop if sumkids>2 | sumkids==0
(346,244 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include data limited to the years 2000 to 2020.
. drop if syear<2000 | syear>2020
(0 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only responses from individuals over the age of 18.
. drop if bioage <18
(73,666 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only Computer-Assisted Personal Interviews (CAPI) to avoid experi
> menter effects \\ QUESTION
. drop if pgmode!=140
(131,929 observations deleted)

.         
.         
. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. *Tidy Control Variables
. rename bioage Age

. rename sex Male

. gen Income = pglabgro if pglabgro>=0
(46,516 missing values generated)

. replace Income = Income + pgsndjob if pgsndjob>0
(2,565 real changes made)

. replace pgnation = . if pgnation==-1
(2 real changes made, 2 to missing)

. rename pgnation Nationality

. gen Partner_In_House = 1 if pld0133==1
(98,711 missing values generated)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==2
(5,645 real changes made)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==-2  
(86,939 real changes made)

. 
. 
. *Dependant variable
. *Our dependent variable will be agreement that men and women should share hou
> sehold responsibilities equally -- "Completely Disagree" (1) to "Fully agree"
>  (7).
. rename plh0308_v2 Equal_responsibility

. drop if Equal_responsibility <0
(103,531 observations deleted)

. 
. *Independant variables
. *We create a binary variable which takes the value 1 if a respondent answers 
> to one or more of the kidsex variables that the sex of their child is 'Female
> ' and '0' otherwise.
. gen At_least_One_Daughter = 0

. foreach var of varlist kidsex01-kidsex02 {
  2.     replace At_least_One_Daughter = 1 if `var' == 2
  3. }
(3,783 real changes made)
(1,277 real changes made)

. 
. *We also consider a pre (0) and post (1) treatment dummy coded as 0 before re
> spondents have a daughter and 1 after respondents have a daughter
. //gen After_Having_Daughter = 0
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex01==2 & (kidgeb01<=syear|syear<2
> 000)
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex02==2 & kidgeb02<=syear
. 
. *To use the Callaway & Sant'Anna (2021) method of staggered DiD as a robustne
> ss check we also generate a variable for the first year respondents had a dau
> ghter
. //gen First_Year_Daughter = .
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb01 if kidsex01==2 & kidgeb01>2000
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb02 if kidsex02==2 & kidsex01!=2 & kidge
> b02>2000
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 *
. *To test our fourth hypothesis that having daughters leads to a larger increa
> se in the support of gender equality for men than for women, we conduct a sta
> ggered difference-in-difference estimation with time (syear) and individual-l
> evel (pid) fixed effects and clustered standard errors, of agreement that men
>  and women should share household responsibilities equally (Equal_responsibil
> ity) on the dummy for having a daughter or not (At_least_One_Daughter), a dum
> my for pre and post having the first daughter (After_Having_Daughter) and a d
> ummy for whether the respondent is Male or Female (Male) and a triple interac
> tion term between the three dummies (At_least_One_Daughter x After_Having_Dau
> ghter x Male).
. //reghdfe Equal_responsibility i.At_least_One_Daughter#i.After_Having_Daughte
> r#i.Male, absorb(pid syear) vce(cluster pid)
. //reghdfe Equal_responsibility i.At_least_One_Daughter##i.After_Having_Daught
> er#i.Male Age Income i.Nationality Partner_In_House sumkids, absorb(pid syear
> ) vce(cluster pid)
. 
. // For robustness we also conduct a staggered diff in diff using the Callaway
>  & Sant'Anna (2021) method to account for treatment effect heterogeneity
. //csdid Equal_responsibility At_least_One_Daughter, ivar(pid) time(syear) gva
> r(First_Year_Daughter) group(Male) method(dripw) vce(cluster pid)
. //csdid Equal_responsibility At_least_One_Daughter Age Income i.Nationality P
> artner_In_House sumkids, ivar(pid) time(syear) gvar(First_Year_Daughter) grou
> p(Male) method(dripw) vce(cluster pid)
.  
. // Panel Analysis not possible because responses to Equal_responsibility were
>  only given in 2018, so we provide the cross-sectional alternative to the ana
> lysis in our preanalysis plan. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 - CROSS-SECTIONAL*
. reg Equal_responsibility At_least_One_Daughter##Male

